","sourceTitle":"David"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"A Psalm of David, when he fled from his son Absalom. O LORD, how my foes have increased! How many rise up against me!","verse":1},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"But You, O LORD, are a shield around me, my glory, and the One who lifts my head.","verse":3},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"To the LORD I cry aloud, and He answers me from His holy mountain. Selah","verse":4},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"I lie down and sleep; I wake again, for the LORD sustains me.","verse":5},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Arise, O LORD! Save me, O my God! Strike all my enemies on the jaw; break the teeth of the wicked.","verse":7},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"Salvation belongs to the LORD; may Your blessing be on Your people. Selah","verse":8}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Salvation","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":8,"href":"?bref=Ps.3.8","rawReference":"Ps.3.8"}],"ruleId":"Salvation::Salvation::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Salvation"},"text":"Salvation belongs to the LORD; may Your blessing be on Your people. Selah","verse":8}],"id":"Salvation","label":"Salvation","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Salvation::Salvation::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Reviewed original headword and source sense. This substantive word is admitted only where the original article explicitly cites the exact occurrence verse; ambiguous homographs and known context mismatches are separately excluded. This is selective contextual evidence, not an automatic rule for every same-spelling word.","sourceHeadwordId":"Salvation","term":"Salvation"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Salvation","sourceTitle":"Salvation"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":["Prayers for Vengeance"],"sourceClass":"theme-title","t":"h"},{"c":["The psalmists sometimes asked the Lord to execute vengeance against their adversaries. It was not unusual for a psalmist to pray for the violent destruction of their enemies as a manifestation of God’s justice. How can this kind of prayer be okay?"],"sourceClass":"theme-body-fl","t":"p"},{"c":["These prayers for the destruction of the wicked arose out of concern for justice and righteousness and out of confidence in God. Divine justice is defined in ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.1.6","r":"Ps.1.6","rawR":"Ps.1.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.1.6","value":"Ps.1.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 1:6"},": The Lord loves the righteous and destroys the wicked. The wicked are subversive, corrupt, and thoroughly committed to evil; they live in opposition to God and to everything that God does. The wicked shake the foundations of ethics, of society, and of God’s kingdom. The psalmists argued that evil is inconsistent with God’s nature and that the removal of evil is the only way for his kingdom to thrive. However, the poets of Israel did not simply invoke God’s judgment on anyone with whom they could not get along. Instead, the psalmists were guided by God’s standards of justice and righteousness, to which God holds all humans accountable."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["The psalmists were intimately acquainted with grief. They had suffered and been oppressed and marginalized by bullies, leaders, and kings from inside and outside of Israel. Their prayers were full of faith and hope, asking how long the Lord would tolerate their suffering and confessing that the Lord alone could rescue them from evil. They expressed deep longing for his redemption. By the principle of retribution, they asked the Lord to inflict upon the wicked the suffering that they had endured (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.10","r":"Ps.5.10","rawR":"Ps.5.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.10","value":"Ps.5.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 5:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.6.10","r":"Ps.6.10","rawR":"Ps.6.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.6.10","value":"Ps.6.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.7.9","r":"Ps.7.9","rawR":"Ps.7.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.7.9","value":"Ps.7.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.9.19-20","r":"Ps.9.19-20","rawR":"Ps.9.19-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.9.19-20","value":"Ps.9.19-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:19-20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.28.4","r":"Ps.28.4","rawR":"Ps.28.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.28.4","value":"Ps.28.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"28:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.56.7","r":"Ps.56.7","rawR":"Ps.56.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.56.7","value":"Ps.56.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"56:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.104.35","r":"Ps.104.35","rawR":"Ps.104.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.104.35","value":"Ps.104.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"104:35"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.137.7-9","r":"Ps.137.7-9","rawR":"Ps.137.7-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.137.7-9","value":"Ps.137.7-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"137:7-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.139.19","r":"Ps.139.19","rawR":"Ps.139.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.139.19","value":"Ps.139.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"139:19"},"). Through these prayers for justice and vindication, the godly may rest in peace as they await God’s rescue."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Do we truly see evil as evil, or do we perceive it merely as an inconvenience? Prayers for the end of evil are appropriate as long as we recognize God as arbiter, judge, and executor. The prayer for the coming of God’s Kingdom implies the removal of evil. But now the cruelty inflicted on the wicked has been transformed through the cruel crucifixion of Jesus Christ. This act of God informs how we pray for those who oppose us. Jesus will indeed judge and bring an ultimate end to evil (see ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.19.11-21","r":"Rev.19.11-21","rawR":"Rev.19.11-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.19.11-21","value":"Rev.19.11-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rev 19:11-21"},"), but while Christians await that final judgment, they are to love as Christ loved (",{"href":"?bref=John.13.34","r":"John.13.34","rawR":"John.13.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.13.34","value":"John.13.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"John 13:34"},"), pray for their enemies, and forgive them (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.5.38-48","r":"Matt.5.38-48","rawR":"Matt.5.38-48","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.5.38-48","value":"Matt.5.38-48"}],"t":"ref","v":"Matt 5:38-48"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Col.3.13","r":"Col.3.13","rawR":"Col.3.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Col.3.13","value":"Col.3.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Col 3:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"theme-body","t":"p"},{"c":["Passages for Further Study"],"sourceClass":"theme-refs-title","t":"h"},{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.24.22","r":"2Chr.24.22","rawR":"2Chr.24.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.24.22","value":"2Chr.24.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 24:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.4.5","r":"Neh.4.5","rawR":"Neh.4.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.4.5","value":"Neh.4.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 4:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.7","r":"Ps.3.7","rawR":"Ps.3.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.7","value":"Ps.3.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 3:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.9.19-20","r":"Ps.9.19-20","rawR":"Ps.9.19-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.9.19-20","value":"Ps.9.19-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:19-20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.10.15","r":"Ps.10.15","rawR":"Ps.10.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.10.15","value":"Ps.10.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.12.3","r":"Ps.12.3","rawR":"Ps.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.12.3","value":"Ps.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.41.10","r":"Ps.41.10","rawR":"Ps.41.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.41.10","value":"Ps.41.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"41:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.55.15","r":"Ps.55.15","rawR":"Ps.55.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.55.15","value":"Ps.55.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"55:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.69.22-28","r":"Ps.69.22-28","rawR":"Ps.69.22-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.69.22-28","value":"Ps.69.22-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"69:22-28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.79.6","r":"Ps.79.6","rawR":"Ps.79.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.79.6","value":"Ps.79.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"79:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.109.6-20","r":"Ps.109.6-20","rawR":"Ps.109.6-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.109.6-20","value":"Ps.109.6-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"109:6-20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.110.5-6","r":"Ps.110.5-6","rawR":"Ps.110.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.110.5-6","value":"Ps.110.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"110:5-6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.137.1-9","r":"Ps.137.1-9","rawR":"Ps.137.1-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.137.1-9","value":"Ps.137.1-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"137:1-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.61.2","r":"Isa.61.2","rawR":"Isa.61.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.61.2","value":"Isa.61.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 61:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.11.20-23","r":"Jer.11.20-23","rawR":"Jer.11.20-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.11.20-23","value":"Jer.11.20-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 11:20-23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.18.19-23","r":"Jer.18.19-23","rawR":"Jer.18.19-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.18.19-23","value":"Jer.18.19-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:19-23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.51.35","r":"Jer.51.35","rawR":"Jer.51.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.51.35","value":"Jer.51.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"51:35"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lam.1.22","r":"Lam.1.22","rawR":"Lam.1.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lam.1.22","value":"Lam.1.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lam 1:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lam.3.64-66","r":"Lam.3.64-66","rawR":"Lam.3.64-66","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lam.3.64-66","value":"Lam.3.64-66"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:64-66"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.1.20","r":"Acts.1.20","rawR":"Acts.1.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.1.20","value":"Acts.1.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 1:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rom.11.9-10","r":"Rom.11.9-10","rawR":"Rom.11.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.11.9-10","value":"Rom.11.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 11:9-10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.6.10","r":"Rev.6.10","rawR":"Rev.6.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.6.10","value":"Rev.6.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rev 6:10"}],"sourceClass":"theme-refs","t":"p"}],"id":"ThemeNote:PrayersForVengeance","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":3,"endVerse":7,"startChapter":3,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"PrayersForVengeance","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"ThemeNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[3],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"38c92b9fac44c39e8f066033abbec3ab25800ef74e85f4c10506b7137a53f664","sourceItemName":"PrayersForVengeance","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/ThemeNotes.xml","sourceOrder":123,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.3.7","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":"Prayers for Vengeance","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Prayers for Vengeance","type":"ThemeNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.1-7.17","r":"Ps.3.1-7.17","rawR":"Ps.3.1-7.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.1-7.17","value":"Ps.3.1-7.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 3–7"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This group of psalms moves readers from the orderly world of ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.1.1-2.12","r":"Ps.1.1-2.12","rawR":"Ps.1.1-2.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.1.1-2.12","value":"Ps.1.1-2.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 1–2"}," to a disoriented one. The Lord’s anointed cries out while facing enemies, ferocious opposition, evil schemes, and the Lord’s apparent distance."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.3.1-7.17","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":7,"endVerse":17,"startChapter":3,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.3.1-7.17","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[3,4,5,6,7],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"979e35739df35cd8a906cb35ce271f91dc796183d42ddf70cbc0fa127889810f","sourceItemName":"Ps.3.1-7.17","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5981,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.3.1-7.17","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.3.1-7.17","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.1-8","r":"Ps.3.1-8","rawR":"Ps.3.1-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.1-8","value":"Ps.3.1-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This psalm laments that the expectations raised by ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.1.1-2.12","r":"Ps.1.1-2.12","rawR":"Ps.1.1-2.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.1.1-2.12","value":"Ps.1.1-2.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 1–2"}," have not been met. But even when beset by enemies, godly people need not question the Lord’s just dealings. Rather, they can confidently trust his goodness and expect God to rescue them."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.3.1-8","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":3,"endVerse":8,"startChapter":3,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.3.1-8","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[3],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"593a05887578cb797b25086e73c0c9a37d373e1050a28881a92d7c215ff7e879","sourceItemName":"Ps.3.1-8","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5982,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.3.1-8","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.3.1-8","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.1","r":"Ps.3.1","rawR":"Ps.3.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.1","value":"Ps.3.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:title"}," This sad episode in David’s life (see ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.15.1-18.33","r":"2Sam.15.1-18.33","rawR":"2Sam.15.1-18.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.15.1-18.33","value":"2Sam.15.1-18.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sam 15–18"},") helps readers keep the promises of ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.2.1-12","r":"Ps.2.1-12","rawR":"Ps.2.1-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.2.1-12","value":"Ps.2.1-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 2"}," in perspective. The Lord granted victory to his anointed king (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.2.1-12","r":"Ps.2.1-12","rawR":"Ps.2.1-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.2.1-12","value":"Ps.2.1-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 2"},"), but the manner and timing of this victory remained in God’s hands."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.3.1","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":3,"endVerse":1,"startChapter":3,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.3.1","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[3],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8797e6c0a1ed843a625418501d2f4722068d3d0f71343bca3555939acea73503","sourceItemName":"Ps.3.1","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5983,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.3.1","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.3.1","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.1-2","r":"Ps.3.1-2","rawR":"Ps.3.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.1-2","value":"Ps.3.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:1-2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist’s ",{"c":["many enemies"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," speak brashly (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.4.6","r":"Ps.4.6","rawR":"Ps.4.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.4.6","value":"Ps.4.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.12.4","r":"Ps.12.4","rawR":"Ps.12.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.12.4","value":"Ps.12.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.40.15","r":"Ps.40.15","rawR":"Ps.40.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.40.15","value":"Ps.40.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"40:15"},") and question the Lord’s ability to rescue (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.10.11","r":"Ps.10.11","rawR":"Ps.10.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.10.11","value":"Ps.10.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.22.7-8","r":"Ps.22.7-8","rawR":"Ps.22.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.22.7-8","value":"Ps.22.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:7-8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.71.10","r":"Ps.71.10","rawR":"Ps.71.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.71.10","value":"Ps.71.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"71:10"},"). Their words haunt him because it seems that the Lord will not answer his prayer. • These enemies wield great power (cp. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.2.1-3","r":"Ps.2.1-3","rawR":"Ps.2.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.2.1-3","value":"Ps.2.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:1-3"},"); unlike ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.2.1-12","r":"Ps.2.1-12","rawR":"Ps.2.1-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.2.1-12","value":"Ps.2.1-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 2"},", this psalm does not resolve the crisis."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.3.1-2","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":3,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":3,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.3.1-2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[3],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f232d045816d31e06537fbf6373bade9d1d4ddbd51ab22bb701a3736ac22fd07","sourceItemName":"Ps.3.1-2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5984,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.3.1-2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.3.1-2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.3-4","r":"Ps.3.3-4","rawR":"Ps.3.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.3-4","value":"Ps.3.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:3-4"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist’s eyes turn from his enemies to the Lord."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.3.3-4","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":3,"endVerse":4,"startChapter":3,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.3.3-4","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[3],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2c66e1a6c9a1d72b0b395053b7a746777bd0c0c8cb2114d49b0bb40f35594586","sourceItemName":"Ps.3.3-4","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5985,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.3.3-4","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.3.3-4","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.3","r":"Ps.3.3","rawR":"Ps.3.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.3","value":"Ps.3.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The psalmist contrasts the contention of his enemies (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.2","r":"Ps.3.2","rawR":"Ps.3.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.2","value":"Ps.3.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:2"},") with the Lord’s provision. The Lord is a ",{"c":["shield"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," for his people; he turns their defeat and shame into victory and ",{"c":["glory"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},"."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.3.3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":3,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":3,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.3.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[3],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"afde37c4c0a6b8a931b0a5a0e25cd5515c233cf2c5b6c8cad8ea592108621508","sourceItemName":"Ps.3.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":5986,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.3.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.3.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.5","r":"Ps.3.5","rawR":"Ps.3.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.5","value":"Ps.3.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:5"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," By refocusing on the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.3.3-4","r":"Ps.3.3-4","rawR":"Ps.3.3-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.3.3-4","value":"Ps.3.3-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:3-4"},") in the midst of his crisis, the psalmist can rest, confident of his ",{"c":["safety"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (see ",{"href":"?item=Ps.4.8_StudyNote_Filament","id":"Ps.4.8_StudyNote_Filament","rawId":"Ps.4.8_StudyNote_Filament","t":"link","v":"study note on 4:8"},"). The Lord cares for his servant; he protects him and keeps his mind and heart from fear (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.37.17","r":"Ps.37.17","rawR":"Ps.37.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.37.17","value":"Ps.37.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"37:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.54.4","r":"Ps.54.4","rawR":"Ps.54.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.54.4","value":"Ps.54.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"54:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.119.116","r":"Ps.119.116","rawR":"Ps.119.116","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.119.116","value":"Ps.119.116"}],"t":"ref","v":"119:116"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.145.14","r":"Ps.145.14","rawR":"Ps.145.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.145.14","value":"Ps.145.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"145:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.3.5","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":3,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":3,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.3.5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[3],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c3480cc68fd4e2c9